.TH C4TUI 1 "May 2026" "c4tui 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
c4tui \- interactive terminal viewer for Structurizr C4 diagrams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B c4tui
[\fB--workspace\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB--structurizr-cli\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB--log-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B c4tui
exports a Structurizr workspace to SVG using structurizr-cli, rasterizes the exported views, and displays them inline in terminals that support the Kitty graphics protocol. It supports view picking, pan/zoom, click-to-drill navigation, breadcrumb backtracking, reload, and an in-terminal help overlay.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --workspace PATH
Path to workspace.dsl, workspace.json, or a directory containing one.
.TP
.B --structurizr-cli PATH
Path to the structurizr-cli executable. Defaults to searching PATH.
.TP
.B --svg-format FORMAT
Structurizr CLI export format. Defaults to svg.
.TP
.B --config PATH
Read configuration from PATH instead of ~/.config/c4tui/config.toml.
.TP
.B --log-file PATH
Write logs to PATH. Select verbosity with RUST_LOG.
.TP
.B --capability-timeout-ms MS
Timeout for terminal capability probes. Defaults to 200.
.TP
.B --force-probe
Print capability results even when stdout is not attached to a terminal.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B ?
Show help.
.TP
.B o
Open the view picker. Use Up/Down and Enter; Esc cancels.
.TP
.B r
Reload the workspace by re-running Structurizr export.
.TP
.B Backspace
Navigate back through breadcrumbs.
.TP
.B +, -
Zoom in and out.
.TP
.B 0, f
Reset/fit the current view.
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Pan the current view.
.TP
.B Mouse wheel / drag / click
Zoom, pan, and drill into child views.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration path is ~/.config/c4tui/config.toml.
.PP
.nf
dpi_scale = 4.0

[keybindings]
quit = "q"
open_picker = "o"
reload = "r"
help = "?"
zoom_in = "+"
zoom_out = "-"
reset = "0"
fit = "f"
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls logging verbosity, for example RUST_LOG=c4tui=debug.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A terminal with Kitty graphics support and structurizr-cli available locally.
